## Required ordering contract

- Emit exactly one top-level `<section data-section-type="activity_ordering" data-section-id="...">`.
- Put the sortable items in one `<ol data-activity-order-list>`.
- Each direct child is one card with a unique `data-activity-item="item-N"`, `tabindex="0"`, and `draggable="true"`.
- Give cards clear muted borders and a child-friendly layout. The runtime adds visible move controls.
- Encode the correct item-id sequence on the section as `data-correct-order="item-2,item-1,..."`.
- The initial DOM order must differ from the correct order unless the textbook explicitly presents a partially completed sequence.
- Every visible source text leaf must preserve its exact text and carry its provided `data-id` exactly once.
- Generated visible labels may use unique `data-id="activity_gen_<slug>"` values.
- Images belonging to an item must be inside that item's card, with the provided image ID and meaningful alt text.
- Do not add custom scripts or inline event handlers.
- The activity must remain understandable without color and at narrow viewport widths.

Example:
```html
<section data-section-type="activity_ordering" data-section-id="pg001_sec001"
         data-correct-order="item-2,item-1,item-4,item-3">
  <p data-id="pg001_q1">Arrange from shortest to tallest.</p>
  <ol data-activity-order-list class="grid gap-3">
    <li data-activity-item="item-1" tabindex="0" draggable="true" class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-xl border-2 border-slate-400 bg-white p-3">
      <span data-id="pg001_o1">Shira — 3626 m</span>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>
```
